# The images of the evaluations, the packs, and the spikes are Git LFS files (crit-yi0).
# Reason: `/plugin marketplace add` clones this whole repository, and these images were
# 114 MB of a 140 MB clone. With `.lfsconfig`, an install gets small pointer files.
# The patterns name folders, so a file under `plugin/` can never become a pointer.
# To get the real images in a development checkout, see "Develop" in README.md.
evals/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
evals/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
packs/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
packs/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
spike/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
spike/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# README.md shows this image, so it stays a plain git file. Reason: nobody has confirmed
# that GitHub renders a README image that is a Git LFS file. Review trigger: README.md
# stops showing it. This line must come after the patterns above.
evals/critic/work-order/bad-page/desktop.png !filter !diff !merge
